    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.assignCustomerCode`.\n\nThe computed code is `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (a pure function of region + telephone + last name). Previously two owners could collide on this value. Now `assignCustomerCode` passes the computed code through a new `deduplicateCustomerCode` helper:\n\n- It gathers the `customerCode`s of all pre-existing owners.\n- If the computed code isn't already taken, it's returned unchanged.\n- Otherwise it appends `-<n>`, starting at `n = 2` and incrementing to the smallest value that isn't already in use, then returns that de-duplicated code.\n\nBecause this runs before `assignMembershipNumber`, the membership number correctly derives from the de-duplicated code.\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `code-collision` acceptance test asserting distinct owners get distinct customer codes passes).",
